istancing could be throttled up and  down depending on the pressure on the  NHS it would work something like this  bring in strict social distancing and  the demand for beds quickly drops  is the restrictions so people can resume  normal life and the demand for hospital  care would rise it would according to  the model potentially save lives and in  small windows allow for fun and lifts  the economy but no public health  intervention with such disruptive effect  on society has ever been attempted for  so long and the scientists warn it will  only work if people make an enormous  social sacrifice
 

